{"page_content": "Descriptor list for Process Categories (PROC)\n\nThe process categories define tasks, or process types from the occupational perspective. The PROCs are also differentiated by taking into account the exposure potential for workers during the respective tasks or process types. This descriptor can be assigned to workers\u2019 activities contributing to a use. The categories are meant to support harmonised and consistent exposure assessment across sectors and supply chains.\n\nThe use descriptor included in the description of use is expected to reflect the nature and scope of the activities. The explanations and examples below should be looked at in order to ensure that the process category assigned is appropriate.\n\nWhen no appropriate descriptor is available \u201cPROC0 - other\u201d should be selected and a description should be provided.\n\nTable R.12- 11: Descriptor list for Process categories (PROC)", "metadata": {"doc_id": "2304b1fd-12fe-49c4-907b-56d174be1ce0", "content_type": "CompositeElement", "filename": "information_requirements_r12_en.pdf"}}